tarred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Independent review verdict for exact head `a8a581623cc45e4cf38a6e66f3a6403a9bfafeaf`: **NOT PASS yet**.\n\nThe committed result evidence is internally consistent on the review host: 13 complete papers / 108 questions / 144 regions / P1-P6 / prior overlap 0; the frozen manifest, truth, runner, prompt, harness, PDF, crop, and rendered-image hashes all verify; the external checkpoint is exactly `2d977275b1db63bea9648e7b246a28567745bbaee95d1e356c05c541ffdf8a02` with 108 unique terminal rows, 216 raw responses, and 0 silent rows; all 108 terminal-row files, 216 request/metadata pairs, 216 raw-response hashes, and 216 rendered-image hashes verify; checkpoint-only recomputation exactly reproduces the four committed compact artifacts and 82/108 first-pass, 98/108 final, 10 residuals. No strong secret pattern was found. The preflight receipt binding manifest/truth/harness predates the first raw response. Focused Python suites pass 5 + 23 + 11 + 24; report-index and diff-check pass. The bundle secret scanner could not execute in this clean review worktree because no `dist/assets` exists, while the live PR trust-boundary check is green.\n\nHowever, the five unresolved exact-head threads identify real harness limitations, and the current report/readback discloses only the compact-artifact reconstruction discrepancy:\n\n1. `prepare` unconditionally rewrites the committed truth and manifest, so the harness itself does not enforce the stated post-response immutability contract.\n2. `--max-retries` is not checked against the manifest or bound into terminal provenance, so the declared retry policy cannot be attributed to an execution/checkpoint. The observed run had one attempt per pass and no retries, so this does not change the measured result.\n3. resume validates provenance fields but does not bind checkpoint rows to immutable terminal-row/raw-response bytes or rescore them before finalization. I verified the current external evidence byte-for-byte, but the generic exact-resume integrity claim is broader than the implementation.\n4. frozen crop validation is pinned to the author's absolute home path and lacks an override/rematerialization path, limiting independent replay off-host.\n5. an accepted relative `--truth` argument is written and then fails during `relative_to(REPO)`, leaving a partial prepare output.\n\nBecause issue #1629 forbids changing the execution harness after responses were observed, do **not** repair or rerun this holdout. Before PASS, update only the non-behavioral report/readback to enumerate these preserved findings, narrow the immutability/exact-resume/replay claims to what is actually evidenced, and create or link a bounded successor investigation. Reply to each unresolved thread, then request a fresh exact-head review. Do not change the frozen harness, manifest, truth, candidate results, or checkpoint.\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1630#pullrequestreview-4732599115","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1630","author_association":"OWNER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1630#pullrequestreview-4732599115"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1630"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-20T06:33:30Z","commit_id":"a8a581623cc45e4cf38a6e66f3a6403a9bfafeaf"},{"id":4732640080,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOO5D6p88AAAABGhZbUA","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node